{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-146394",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "If $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables with the joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then the corresponding joint CDF is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)={\\sum }_{{x}_{i}\\le x}{\\sum }_{{y}_{i}\\le y}f({x}_{i},{y}_{i}).\n$$\n\nBy definition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0,\\frac{3}{2}) & =P(X\\le 0,Y\\le \\frac{3}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by highlighting all cells in the table that correspond to $X\\le 0,Y\\le \\frac{3}{2}.$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=-1$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0,\\frac{3}{2}) & ={\\sum }_{x\\le 0}{\\sum }_{y\\le 3/2}f(x,y) \\\\  & =f(-1,-1)+f(-1,0)+f(-1,1) \\\\  & =0.15+0.25+0.05 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
